                  , MLM, “Agda”
          %p The sections of the table corresponds roughly to the kinds of reasoning captured by the systems:
          %ul
            %li Finitistic reasoning about the natural numbers (and other finitistic inductive types)
            %li Predicative reasoning about the natural numbers
            %li Meta-predicative reasoning about the natural numbers
            %li Reasoning about general inductive types
            %li Reasoning about general inductive-recursive types
          %p Note that these are all very much weaker than full second-order arithmetic, and of course much weaker than Zermelo or Zermelo-Fraenkel set theory.
          %p After the meta-predicative systems, all ordinals use a notation which refers to a much larger ordinal, often patterned on a large cardinal.
          %p
            Rathjen (2005) analyzed systems up to
            = succeed "-CA+BI+" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
